## The Infinite Descent

```xiom
fn factorial(n: Int) -> Int {
  return n * factorial(n - 1);  // No base case! Stack overflow!
}
```

### Mandatory Base Case
```xiom
fn factorial(n: Int) -> Int
  requires: n >= 0;
  ensures: result > 0;
{
  if n <= 1 { return 1; }           // Base case!
  return n * factorial(n - 1);
}
```

### Tail Recursion (Stack-Safe)
```xiom
fn factorial_tail(n: Int, acc: Int) -> Int
  requires: n >= 0;
{
  if n <= 1 { return acc; }
  return factorial_tail(n - 1, acc * n);  // Tail call: reuses stack frame
}

fn factorial(n: Int) -> Int {
  return factorial_tail(n, 1);
}
```

The compiler can optimize tail-recursive calls to loops — no stack growth.

### Iterative Alternative
```xiom
fn factorial_iter(n: Int) -> Int
  requires: n >= 0;
{
  var result = 1;
  for i in 1..=n { result = result * i; }
  return result;
}
```

